  "body": "What happens: on upstream main, the ui lib test `diag::tests::shared_ui_code_prints_only_through_the_diag_seam` fails. It flags the `eprintln!` at `crates/ui/src/egui_app/app_icon.rs:25`, in `window_icon()`'s error arm. That line came in with 24fd40cb (\"feat(ui): logotype as window icon, generated sizes, README and site favicon\").\n\nFound while refreshing PR #1472: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=1` gives 690 passed and 1 failed. The PR touches neither `app_icon.rs` nor `diag.rs`; both are byte-identical to upstream main.\n\nExpected: shared UI code logs through the diag seam (the law the test enforces), so the \"window opens without an icon\" line goes through `diag` like the other UI logs, and the test is green.\n\nDone means: `window_icon()` logs through the diag seam, `shared_ui_code_prints_only_through_the_diag_seam` passes on main, and the ui lib is green.\n",
